## Branch cut (mandatory)

Every proof branch must be cut from upstream `open-goat/pequalnp-proofs` main so this fork's `.cursor/` files never appear in a proof PR. PRs must contain exactly one Lean file.

```
git fetch upstream
git checkout -b <gap id> upstream/main
```

If `upstream` is missing: `git remote add upstream https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs.git`

Do not branch from this fork's `main`, and do not include `.cursor/`, install scripts, or rules in a proof PR.

## Lean file

One file: `lean/PEqualNP/Outside/L_<gap>.lean` (lowercase letters, digits, underscores). One theorem named after the module, last in the file, full name. Helpers only inside `namespace <module> ... end <module>` (or `_aux` / a name below either). Imports only `Mathlib`, Mathlib modules, and `gap.imports`. The word `import` appears only in the import lines at the top.

Forbidden: `sorry`; new `axiom`; `native_decide`; any `#` command (`#eval` and the rest); `macro` / `syntax` / `notation` / `elab`; string literals (no double quotes anywhere); `initialize`; `attribute` commands. Options: only `set_option maxHeartbeats N in`, `set_option maxRecDepth N in`, `set_option synthInstance.maxSize N in`, `set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats N in`, each on its own line directly above the declaration it serves. Attributes: only `@[simp]` and `@[local simp]`.

Prove the posted statement exactly. If it is false, prove the desk's negated twin (`It is false that ...`) when that twin exists; otherwise prove `¬ (posted statement)` and submit with checker kind `refute`. Do not rewrite the statement.

Before submit: `lake build <gap.module>` and `node tools/check-lean.mjs <lean file> <statement file> [check|refute]` must pass.

## Pull requests

Open into `open-goat/pequalnp-proofs`. Title is exactly the gap id (for example `L-meta-2232`). Use the default PR template from `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` **without** the X handle and LinkedIn lines. Fill Gap id, the one file path, Agent used (`Cursor`), and the checklist. Do not add extra files.

## Search and circuit steps

For search shards and small-circuit existence/refutation, use `kissat` and/or `cadical` to find a witness or prove unsat, then have Lean verify the certificate with `decide` (never `native_decide`). Keep SAT work out of the proof PR; only the Lean file is submitted. `.cursor/tools/open_steps.sh` lists desk gaps with no open/merged PR, easiest first. `.cursor/templates/SmallCircuit.lean` is a `decide` circuit sketch; `.cursor/examples/` holds copied accepted proofs of the same kind. Paste `.cursor/lib/CircuitKit.lean` (BEGIN/END) via `.cursor/tools/new_proof.sh`; never put `.cursor/` on a proof branch. The kit must not declare a new data type. Run `.cursor/tools/precheck.sh <file>` (or `.cursor/tools/new_steps.sh --push <file>`) before every push.

## Desk

Work only on a step with a live lease. Renew with `tools/pnp.sh beat <step>` (or the desk `beat` URL) while working. Do not open issues or PRs that are not a proof of the held step.
